{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "identify y'' + y = 0:\n  an ordinary differential equation of order 2 in y(t)\n  linear: every y-term appears to the first power [proved: the partial derivatives in y, y', ... do not involve y]\n  homogeneous\n  constant coefficients (and autonomous)\n  characteristic equation: r^2 + 1 = 0, roots ±i\n  homogeneous solutions: y(t) = a combination of cos(t), sin(t)\n  autonomous: the independent variable does not appear explicitly\n  solved for the highest derivative: y'' = -y  (then initial values and: dsolve y)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "identify", "ucas": "identify y'' + y = 0", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "identify", "input": "y'' + y = 0", "properties": {"linear": {"text": "every y-term appears to the first power", "tag": "proved: the partial derivatives in y, y', ... do not involve y", "proof": "symbolic"}, "characteristic_equation": "r^2 + 1 = 0, roots ±i", "homogeneous_solutions": "y(t) = a combination of cos(t), sin(t)", "autonomous": "the independent variable does not appear explicitly", "solved_for_the_highest_derivative": "y'' = -y  (then initial values and: dsolve y)", "details": ["an ordinary differential equation of order 2 in y(t)", "homogeneous", "constant coefficients (and autonomous)"]}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "identify y'' + y = 0:\n  an ordinary differential equation of order 2 in y(t)\n  linear: every y-term appears to the first power [proved: the partial derivatives in y, y', ... do not involve y]\n  homogeneous\n  constant coefficients (and autonomous)\n  characteristic equation: r^2 + 1 = 0, roots ±i\n  homogeneous solutions: y(t) = a combination of cos(t), sin(t)\n  autonomous: the independent variable does not appear explicitly\n  solved for the highest derivative: y'' = -y  (then initial values and: dsolve y)\n"}, "isError": false}}
